# Mockito 5's default "inline" mock maker installs a Java agent at
# runtime via Byte Buddy's self-attach. Under JDK 24+ that
# self-attach is restricted, so Mockito.mock(...) can throw without
# -javaagent being passed to the JVM — and jawelte's
# MockitoMockFactory catches that exception and returns null, so
# the auto-mock synthetic bean is never registered and the
# @Inject site fails with UnsatisfiedResolutionException at
# container boot.
#
# Selecting the subclass mock maker below sidesteps that: Byte
# Buddy generates a subclass for each mocked type — no agent
# needed. It mocks interfaces and any non-final class, which
# covers every target jawelte's auto-mock layer hands to Mockito
# (final JDK classes like String / Integer / Class are filtered out
# upstream and never reach the mock factory).

mock-maker-subclass
